  "FIG Code of Points (execution is scored): the salto is judged pass or fail on the rotation, the feet-first landing and the stand, because the task is a single action without a judging panel",
  "the Code of Points has no number for a completed salto; here the pelvis must have turned 300.0 degrees backwards between lift-off and the first touch (a full turn less the backward lean at lift-off and the forward lean a salto still has when its feet touch down); the feet-first landing and the stand judge the rest"
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Do a standing backflip: jump, turn backwards through a full turn in the air, land on your feet and stand.",
  "rules": "The flip is one flight phase (nothing of you touches the ground) of at least 0.2 s that starts from your feet (at lift-off the last things on the ground were your feet, nothing else); shorter hops are ignored, and your first flight of at least 0.2 s is your attempt. The turn is measured on your pelvis: the angle it rotates backwards (head going back, feet coming forward) about the horizontal axis that was its left-right axis at lift-off, added up from lift-off while you are in the air; a rotation on the ground and a twist about the vertical do not count. It must reach 300.0 degrees before anything touches the ground (a full turn less the backward lean a standing take-off already has when the feet leave the ground and the lean a salto still has when its feet touch down: the landing and the stand have to finish the turn). The first touch after the flight must be with the feet only. You then stand for 2.0 s without a break: only your feet on the ground, your torso within 20.0 degrees of vertical, your pelvis slower than 0.35 m/s. You fail if the attempt did not start from the feet alone, if it lands with less than 300.0 degrees turned, if it lands on anything but the feet, if you fall at any time (a fall is: a part of you other than a foot touches the ground, or your pelvis is lower than 0.2 m; a crouch above that is not a fall), or after 20 s.",
  "venue": "You stand in the middle of a floor-exercise area, 12.0 m by 12.0 m, flat, level and rigid, with nothing on it.",
  "difficulty": "A full backward turn needs about 0.6 s of flight with a fast rotation, from legs whose motors give 88 to 139 N m, and a landing on the feet that stops the rotation. No built-in action jumps at all."
 },
